## Frame pipeline (CasparCG-aligned критический путь)

```
Control WS: take / update / clear
  → backend OnAirManager (in-memory + SQLite on_air + fan-out)
  → /ws/renderer?channel=<id> → ChannelClient (bg-runtime.js)
  → TemplateRenderer × N (DOM/CSS mixer — z-order, transforms, blend, masks)
  → CEF HTML Producer compositor (CPU Skia raster, channel-paced rAF)
  → CefRenderHandler::OnPaint(BGRA)
  → FrameRing (SPSC latest-frame)
  → Consumer(s): DeckLink (scheduled) | ffmpeg | preview | null
```

**Почему это соответствует CasparCG-перфу:** та же фундаментальная цепочка CEF OSR → raw pixels → DeckLink scheduled playback. Нет Electron GPU readback/IPC. BGRA native для DeckLink. 1080i50: progressive render @ 50fps → interlaced weave (UFF). Channel-synced animation clock.

## Process model (§4.3)

| Process | Count | Role |
|---|---|---|
| `backend` | 1 | API, WS hub, DB, media jobs |
| `frontend` (dev) / static (prod) | 1 | UI |
| `bg_engine` | 1 per channel | CEF render + output |
| `ffmpeg` (child) | 0–1 per engine | только если stream consumer active |

**CPU affinity:** каждый `bg_engine` pinned к non-overlapping core set через `taskset`/`CPUAffinity`. **Правило: 2 dedicated физических cores на канал** (минимум), без SCHED_RR/RT priority (RT throttling делает хуже — §11.3).

